    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d65">

                <pb facs="0201" n="189" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg189"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to
                        Lieutenant General Albert C.
                    Wedemeyer</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-01-15">15 January 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. Refer your 20060: I am proposing to Generalissimo immediate issue of public
                    order for demilitarization of a certain number of <pb facs="0202" n="190"
                        xml:id="pg190"/> divisions during next 6 months, stating rather precisely
                    the schedule. Also indicating that further demilitarization and demobilization
                    will follow.</p>
                <p>How many divisions might be nominated for next 6 months? Rush reply.</p>
                <p>Farther reference your 20060: please give me a concise statement of matter
                    reference Sixth Army incident and including your general view on demobilization
                    that I can quote to Generalissimo.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
